steps.prompt:
Add a test, in the app's existing test runner and folder, adapted from `.claude/skills/store-screenshots/templates/screenshot-seed-excluded.test.example.ts`. It must fail when:

- the seed module no longer exists;
- `metro.config.js` stops declaring `SCREENSHOT_SEED_MODULE` with the same specifier the app imports, or stops checking `process.env.{{screenshotSeedEnv}} === "1"`, or stops returning `{ type: "empty" }` for it;
- any file other than the entry file and the module itself mentions `screenshot-seed`;
- the switch turns on anything else.

Run the test and make sure it passes. Then record the test's path in `seed.test` of `store-shots.config.mjs`.

In `{{storeShotsAppDir}}/package.json`:

- add `playwright-core` as a dev dependency with the package manager the app already uses (never a downloaded browser: the scripts drive the installed Chrome from `CHROME_PATH`);
- add `"store:shots"` running `node <path to the skill>/scripts/web-preview.mjs` and `"store:frames"` running `node <path to the skill>/scripts/frames.mjs`, with paths relative to the app folder;
- add `{{storeAssetsDir}}/raw/` to the app's `.gitignore` (the bare captures are rebuilt every run; the framed ones may be committed).

Then run `node <path to the skill>/scripts/capture.mjs --validate all`, fix what it reports, and finally run `bun run store:shots` (or the npm/yarn/pnpm equivalent) once. Show the user where the pictures are and ask them to look at every one before uploading anything.
